Suggests:
 openrgb (>= 1.0),
Description: Wild OS lighting
 Sets RGB keyboards, mice and other USB lighting to the colour and effect
 of the taskbar underglow, through OpenRGB, when Settings has it turned on.
 .
 It also runs the effects chosen on Cooler's Lighting page: one effect
 across every part or one for a part on its own, with each zone's name,
 shape and number of lights kept on this PC. Cooler asks for these over the
 session bus (io.wildos.Lighting); this program is the only one that sets a
 light, and it sends moving effects only to a part's Direct mode, which is
 not saved to the part.
 .
 OpenRGB's server runs only while the lighting is on and the session is in
 front, and listens on the loopback only. OpenRGB's own udev rules are
 replaced with narrower ones: the person at the screen gets the hidraw
 nodes of supported USB devices, except those that report key presses, and
 nothing else.
